1
00:00:00,041 --> 00:00:01,540
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,541 --> 00:00:03,041
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:05,333
(Episode 78)

4
00:00:18,083 --> 00:00:22,095
But are you really her mother?
You look more like her sister.

5
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,633
I heard that a lot
when she was in college.

6
00:00:29,766 --> 00:00:31,724
People said we looked
like sisters together.

7
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:39,750
Class isn't something you acquire.
You're born with it.

8
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:44,375
Mom, please be quiet.

9
00:00:44,416 --> 00:00:47,666
What? I like being told I look young.

10
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:49,799
I think this is enough.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,375
You could do a little more...

12
00:00:53,375 --> 00:00:54,632
That's enough.

13
00:00:54,689 --> 00:00:57,750
There's no need to dress up for a funeral.

14
00:01:02,783 --> 00:01:05,574
Take your time with your pretty sister.

15
00:01:05,877 --> 00:01:07,232
Yes, Mother.

16
00:01:07,629 --> 00:01:09,186
Take good care of your little sister.

17
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:11,125
Yes. Please go ahead.

18
00:01:15,573 --> 00:01:18,069
Don't worry.
There aren't two suns in the sky.

19
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:20,706
You're the only one who needs to shine.

20
00:01:21,625 --> 00:01:22,875
Keep an eye on Ji Hu.

21
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:25,208
- Mom!
- Goodness, you startled me.

22
00:01:25,625 --> 00:01:28,250
It's my first time at a wedding,
so I'm really excited.

23
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:31,708
It's okay. You must've been startled.

24
00:01:32,958 --> 00:01:34,208
I'm sorry.

25
00:01:36,143 --> 00:01:38,934
Honestly, you're a mother who's made me
apologize my whole life.

26
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,583
That ends today.

27
00:01:44,916 --> 00:01:46,333
(Don't pick up)

28
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:09,500
The person you are calling is unavailable.
Please leave a message...

29
00:02:45,541 --> 00:02:47,416
(Joong Bin and Sun Kyung's son Lim Ji Hu,
Min Ki and Se Ri's daughter Na Ji Ni)

30
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,665
(Lim Ji Hu, Na Ji Ni)

31
00:03:21,666 --> 00:03:23,488
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

32
00:03:23,708 --> 00:03:26,041
Assemblyman, thank you for coming.

33
00:03:26,083 --> 00:03:28,083
- Thank you for taking the time to come.
- Congratulations.

34
00:03:28,125 --> 00:03:29,958
Thank you.

35
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,041
You've come a long way.

36
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:34,541
- You raised a wonderful son.
- Thank you.

37
00:03:35,422 --> 00:03:36,797
I'm so happy.

38
00:03:39,916 --> 00:03:43,045
Hey, Seung Hyun. Come stand beside me.

39
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:45,458
Didn't you ask me to collect
the cash gifts?

40
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,083
Seung Woo can do that.

41
00:03:47,416 --> 00:03:48,916
It's embarrassing
in front of Ji Hu's family.

42
00:03:50,607 --> 00:03:52,107
There were plenty of people
at the funeral.

43
00:03:52,583 --> 00:03:55,103
A lot of people changed after the funeral.

44
00:03:56,458 --> 00:03:58,291
That damn paperwork...

45
00:04:00,208 --> 00:04:02,333
Yeong Ju, Sa Bin.

46
00:04:02,791 --> 00:04:06,791
We've known each other for 15 years.
You should stand with the bride's side.

47
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:10,666
We should be with Sa Bin's family.
Take care.

48
00:04:13,330 --> 00:04:15,330
Congratulations.

49
00:04:17,199 --> 00:04:18,456
Congratulations.

50
00:04:21,951 --> 00:04:23,240
Okay, look this way, please.

51
00:04:23,241 --> 00:04:25,242
Give us a big smile. One, two.

52
00:04:26,439 --> 00:04:27,541
All done.

53
00:04:27,583 --> 00:04:29,333
- Thank you.
- Congratulations.

54
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:36,041
- Ji Ni, you look gorgeous.
- You're here?

55
00:04:37,666 --> 00:04:39,958
I never thought you'd be the first
of us to get married.

56
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,500
Me neither.

57
00:04:41,583 --> 00:04:44,875
Okay, look this way. Here we go. One, two.

58
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:49,208
Thank you.

59
00:05:07,691 --> 00:05:09,468
That student is here again.

60
00:05:10,706 --> 00:05:13,060
Should I send him away?
He seems a little strange.

61
00:05:13,291 --> 00:05:18,208
Ever since he quit the cello,
he's been acting weird.

62
00:05:18,541 --> 00:05:19,680
I'll go.

63
00:05:51,556 --> 00:05:53,881
I'm sorry, but...

64
00:05:53,958 --> 00:05:55,576
when did you get hurt?

65
00:05:57,797 --> 00:05:58,838
When I was a kid.

66
00:06:05,791 --> 00:06:08,333
Someone's leg was ruined because of you.

67
00:06:22,708 --> 00:06:24,000
What are you doing here?

68
00:06:26,701 --> 00:06:29,201
Are you that nervous?
You're as pale as a ghost.

69
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:38,208
Your mom's here. Hurry, go see her.

70
00:06:42,899 --> 00:06:44,566
That's him, right?
The boy from the accident?

71
00:06:44,764 --> 00:06:45,931
What do you mean, him?

72
00:06:50,194 --> 00:06:51,249
Is that the woman?

73
00:06:51,527 --> 00:06:54,069
The woman you've wanted
to torment your whole life?

74
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:57,166
You really...

75
00:07:05,375 --> 00:07:06,833
Why are you here?

76
00:07:06,916 --> 00:07:08,333
Just came to have a look.

77
00:07:08,958 --> 00:07:11,221
Looks like your daughter's husband
is doing pretty well.

78
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:12,275
Look at all those flower stands.

79
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:16,291
Go near my daughter, and I'll kill you.

80
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:18,321
But I want to apologize.

81
00:07:18,482 --> 00:07:20,851
Seeing his leg like that
makes me feel bad.

82
00:07:22,166 --> 00:07:23,208
Just leave.

83
00:07:23,666 --> 00:07:26,291
You wouldn't let me apologize then,
and you won't let me now.

84
00:07:26,625 --> 00:07:29,166
They even came to your daughter's wedding.
They're good people.

85
00:07:29,208 --> 00:07:31,000
You've been too harsh.

86
00:07:32,791 --> 00:07:35,290
- What?
- If you won't let me apologize,

87
00:07:35,291 --> 00:07:36,833
you should pay me.

88
00:07:37,588 --> 00:07:40,880
I have nothing right now.
I'm living under someone else's roof.

89
00:07:42,041 --> 00:07:43,083
Really?

90
00:07:44,995 --> 00:07:46,870
Then is this plastic?

91
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:49,399
Seriously...

92
00:07:49,866 --> 00:07:52,458
Here. Happy now?

93
00:07:52,875 --> 00:07:54,208
Take it and get lost.

94
00:08:00,601 --> 00:08:03,434
Why are you being so rough?
You're irritating me.

95
00:08:03,575 --> 00:08:05,584
You should've answered my calls, then.

96
00:08:05,937 --> 00:08:08,479
Want me to make a huge scene
in front of everyone here?

97
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,939
Fine. I'm sorry.

98
00:08:10,969 --> 00:08:13,333
I'll answer your calls. Just please leave.

99
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:14,875
Just go.

100
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:17,000
Okay, I said I would.

101
00:08:30,819 --> 00:08:31,972
Good afternoon, everyone.

102
00:08:31,973 --> 00:08:36,361
To all our guests who have taken time
out of their busy schedules to be here,

103
00:08:36,375 --> 00:08:38,750
thank you sincerely for attending
this beautiful wedding.

104
00:08:46,605 --> 00:08:48,063
Are you having a stroke?

105
00:08:48,201 --> 00:08:50,076
Stay still. Why are you shaking so much?

106
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:51,458
Okay.

107
00:08:54,708 --> 00:08:59,208
We will now begin the wedding ceremony
of Lim Ji Hu and Na Ji Ni.

108
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:01,708
Let's get this happy ceremony started!

109
00:09:04,375 --> 00:09:05,922
First,

110
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:09,376
the mothers of the bride and groom
will light the ceremonial candles.

111
00:09:32,622 --> 00:09:35,539
And now, today's star,

112
00:09:35,617 --> 00:09:39,367
the world's most handsome groom
will make his entrance!

113
00:09:39,458 --> 00:09:41,791
Here comes the groom!

114
00:09:45,791 --> 00:09:48,208
Let's give him a big round of applause!

115
00:09:51,708 --> 00:09:53,765
You can tell he's the General's son!

116
00:09:53,913 --> 00:09:56,051
By the way, the groom and I...

117
00:09:56,052 --> 00:09:58,871
have been best friends since daycare,
back in the Sunshine Class.

118
00:10:16,125 --> 00:10:19,041
Now, for the real star of the day,

119
00:10:19,083 --> 00:10:22,750
let's welcome
the world's most beautiful bride!

120
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:26,121
Here comes the bride!

121
00:10:59,958 --> 00:11:01,500
You can go ahead now.

122
00:11:13,581 --> 00:11:15,831
We seem to have a small problem.

123
00:11:15,833 --> 00:11:20,583
Please wait while we resolve the issue.
We apologize for the inconvenience.

124
00:11:25,265 --> 00:11:26,307
Ji Ni.

125
00:12:05,018 --> 00:12:08,093
Here comes the bride, one step at a time.

126
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:10,179
Please give her a warm round of applause.

127
00:12:12,909 --> 00:12:15,888
It seems even the universe
wanted to bless these two...

128
00:12:15,905 --> 00:12:18,739
with a special display of its own.

129
00:12:20,283 --> 00:12:25,200
All your love has lit the way
for our bride.

130
00:12:26,666 --> 00:12:28,791
Let's give them a big round of applause!

131
00:13:02,126 --> 00:13:04,585
Bride and groom, please bow to each other.

132
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:17,751
Ji Ni.

133
00:13:20,153 --> 00:13:24,069
I don't know why seeing you
in your wedding dress makes me cry.

134
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:28,890
You've always had so many fears
and such a kind heart.

135
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,944
Now, don't be afraid.

136
00:13:32,116 --> 00:13:35,876
Face the world with courage
and follow your dreams.

137
00:13:36,622 --> 00:13:39,954
Ji Hu's love and my friendship...

138
00:13:40,279 --> 00:13:42,250
will always support and protect you.

139
00:13:44,125 --> 00:13:47,041
I wish you both happiness. I love you.

140
00:14:05,958 --> 00:14:11,000
<i>I see myself in your eyes</i>

141
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:18,083
<i>The sadness no one else could see</i>

142
00:14:19,333 --> 00:14:24,583
<i>I feel it in your silence</i>

143
00:14:25,369 --> 00:14:31,506
<i>We found love through shared pain</i>

144
00:14:32,604 --> 00:14:37,488
<i>I dream those lost dreams again</i>

145
00:14:39,081 --> 00:14:45,614
<i>And in those dreams I love you</i>

146
00:14:46,117 --> 00:14:51,201
<i>You are my one reason</i>

147
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:58,375
<i>Even when the world comes crashing down</i>
<i>I'll keep holding your hand</i>

148
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:04,583
<i>You are my one reason</i>

149
00:15:04,882 --> 00:15:08,728
<i>A light through endless darkness</i>

150
00:15:09,042 --> 00:15:15,253
<i>This love is my reason</i>

151
00:15:39,541 --> 00:15:42,166
(Valuation loss 1,848.05 dollars,
Return -92.40 percent)

152
00:15:51,015 --> 00:15:52,140
Thank you.

153
00:15:53,612 --> 00:15:54,945
Get some rest too, Su Yeon.

154
00:15:55,291 --> 00:15:56,333
Okay.

155
00:16:04,444 --> 00:16:05,918
The girl who gave the speech today,

156
00:16:07,255 --> 00:16:09,088
she's really nice, isn't she?

157
00:16:09,348 --> 00:16:10,432
Jung A?

158
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:13,998
She's elegant and well put together.

159
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,250
I thought so too.

160
00:16:19,423 --> 00:16:21,881
You've put so much into all of this.

161
00:16:22,787 --> 00:16:23,828
What's this?

162
00:16:29,958 --> 00:16:33,333
You said sapphires suited you.

163
00:16:33,666 --> 00:16:36,583
Go easy on Ji Ni's mom for Ji Hu's sake.

164
00:16:38,984 --> 00:16:41,819
Thank you. You've done so much too.

165
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:46,047
Honey, let's be good parents-in-law.

166
00:16:47,976 --> 00:16:51,198
I want that too, but...

167
00:16:51,458 --> 00:16:53,214
Just look where they went
for their honeymoon.

168
00:16:53,442 --> 00:16:56,525
I never knew Ji Ni had panic disorder.

169
00:16:56,691 --> 00:16:59,067
How bad must it be if she can't even fly?

170
00:16:59,769 --> 00:17:04,310
It breaks my heart that they ended up
going to Sokcho for their honeymoon.

171
00:17:04,403 --> 00:17:07,098
Don't blame her for being sick.
Ji Hu was sick too.

172
00:17:07,389 --> 00:17:09,847
Let's just be thankful today.

173
00:17:10,833 --> 00:17:13,615
How about an evening out
with Sa Bin and Yeong Ju?

174
00:17:13,826 --> 00:17:15,083
We can go to karaoke.

175
00:17:15,970 --> 00:17:17,162
Karaoke?

176
00:17:17,373 --> 00:17:20,373
You can't sing,
so why do you love it so much?

177
00:17:20,375 --> 00:17:22,079
Just come with me this once.

178
00:17:27,865 --> 00:17:30,838
Enough. Please stop.

179
00:18:02,922 --> 00:18:05,501
We should head home too. Get up.

180
00:18:06,515 --> 00:18:07,557
I don't want to.

181
00:18:07,583 --> 00:18:10,166
They get to go on a honeymoon,
but I have to go home?

182
00:18:10,458 --> 00:18:11,708
It's not fair.

183
00:18:13,750 --> 00:18:17,750
Ji Ni's big brother, what's your type?

184
00:18:17,958 --> 00:18:21,083
Do you have a girlfriend?
Do you want me to set you up?

185
00:18:21,694 --> 00:18:24,694
She's really drunk. Hey.

186
00:18:26,333 --> 00:18:29,448
Right, you're married.

187
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:32,750
So what's your type?
Do you want me to set you up?

188
00:18:32,791 --> 00:18:33,981
Really?

189
00:18:35,041 --> 00:18:37,040
Forget it.

190
00:18:37,875 --> 00:18:41,873
I'm not ready to meet someone new yet.

191
00:18:41,875 --> 00:18:43,791
So there's someone you like?

192
00:18:45,598 --> 00:18:47,838
I'm always stuck in unrequited love.

193
00:18:48,889 --> 00:18:50,689
Even back in college,

194
00:18:51,233 --> 00:18:54,972
Ji Ni was busy rejecting guys,
and I was busy chasing them.

195
00:18:57,816 --> 00:18:59,607
Don't you think that's unfair?

196
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:02,953
What's so different about Ji Ni and me?

197
00:19:03,041 --> 00:19:05,291
Tell me, objectively.

198
00:19:05,333 --> 00:19:06,833
Hey, pull yourself together.

199
00:19:07,492 --> 00:19:09,701
Don't mind her, Seung Hyun.

200
00:19:15,286 --> 00:19:16,440
Yes, ma'am.

201
00:19:17,622 --> 00:19:18,622
What?

202
00:19:19,250 --> 00:19:21,788
Okay. Goodbye.

203
00:19:23,307 --> 00:19:26,640
Did you bring Ji Ni's mom's bag?

204
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:28,791
Her bag?

205
00:19:31,043 --> 00:19:32,543
It's in your car.

206
00:19:33,041 --> 00:19:34,717
You're such a pain.

207
00:19:34,956 --> 00:19:36,708
Get up. Let's return it and go home.

208
00:19:36,914 --> 00:19:39,331
Good thing you didn't drink. Take care.

209
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:41,713
Thanks. Hey, let's go.

210
00:19:44,722 --> 00:19:45,790
Hurry up.

211
00:19:47,375 --> 00:19:48,750
Goodbye.

212
00:19:56,496 --> 00:19:57,496
Mai,

213
00:19:58,543 --> 00:20:00,303
it's been months already.

214
00:20:17,041 --> 00:20:21,375
(Today, I feel let down by you.)

215
00:20:34,062 --> 00:20:38,402
Where on earth are you?
What are you doing?

216
00:21:15,875 --> 00:21:17,791
The person you're calling
can't take your call...

217
00:21:18,970 --> 00:21:21,845
What's my mom doing? She's not answering.

218
00:21:23,232 --> 00:21:25,274
Try calling your dad first.

219
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:26,583
Okay.

220
00:21:34,833 --> 00:21:38,000
The person you're calling can't take
your call. Please leave a message...

221
00:21:38,041 --> 00:21:39,245
He's not answering either.

222
00:21:39,672 --> 00:21:43,005
What? I guess neither side
is thinking about us.

223
00:21:45,125 --> 00:21:47,417
Ji Ni, you've got me.

224
00:21:52,375 --> 00:21:53,667
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

225
00:22:00,916 --> 00:22:02,666
You must be hungry after all that singing.

226
00:22:03,253 --> 00:22:04,332
Go ahead and eat.

227
00:22:04,333 --> 00:22:06,458
- That looks delicious. Thanks, Yeong Ju.
- You're welcome.

228
00:22:07,194 --> 00:22:10,791
Sa Bin, enjoy your meal too.

229
00:22:10,833 --> 00:22:12,291
Thanks.

230
00:22:18,992 --> 00:22:21,935
(My son)

231
00:22:22,875 --> 00:22:23,875
Jung A.

232
00:22:24,668 --> 00:22:28,250
Every love feels like a first love.

233
00:22:28,291 --> 00:22:31,000
Love isn't first come, first served.

234
00:22:31,155 --> 00:22:34,531
It's about how deeply you love someone.

235
00:22:35,208 --> 00:22:38,808
Can you keep your eyes on one person
for 20 or 30 years?

236
00:22:38,914 --> 00:22:40,500
That's what matters.

237
00:22:40,875 --> 00:22:43,458
I'd bet my life on that.

238
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:45,078
That's beautiful, ma'am.

239
00:22:45,958 --> 00:22:49,666
- "Love isn't first come, first served."
- Exactly.

240
00:22:49,958 --> 00:22:52,333
- So cutting in line is allowed, then?
- Yeah.

241
00:22:52,583 --> 00:22:54,342
Of course.

242
00:22:55,166 --> 00:22:57,708
Why aren't those kids calling?

243
00:23:00,666 --> 00:23:06,041
They called.

244
00:23:08,278 --> 00:23:10,183
My son-in-law.

245
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:12,958
Yeah, my son-in-law.

246
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,754
Yeah. Did you call?

247
00:23:16,041 --> 00:23:18,020
I'm drunk.

248
00:23:18,306 --> 00:23:20,469
I'm so happy,

249
00:23:20,470 --> 00:23:24,333
so overjoyed I could die!

250
00:23:24,375 --> 00:23:25,958
We've had a drink too.

251
00:23:27,191 --> 00:23:28,232
What were we just doing?

252
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:32,291
We were talking about what Ji Ni
wants to paint next.

253
00:23:33,331 --> 00:23:36,998
That's right.
Ji Ni's passionate about art.

254
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,041
- Let me talk to her.
- Okay.

255
00:23:38,666 --> 00:23:41,208
Mom, why didn't you answer earlier?

256
00:23:41,875 --> 00:23:42,916
With Jung A?

257
00:23:43,750 --> 00:23:47,619
I'm losing it.
You're slurring your words again.

258
00:23:48,505 --> 00:23:50,047
Stop drinking and send her home.

259
00:23:51,125 --> 00:23:52,333
Ji Hu's father?

260
00:23:53,338 --> 00:23:55,297
Of course. We called him.

261
00:23:56,041 --> 00:23:58,541
- Okay.
- Let me talk to her.

262
00:24:00,005 --> 00:24:04,338
Mother, thank you for giving me
your lovely daughter.

263
00:24:04,533 --> 00:24:07,283
I love you. Yes.

264
00:24:09,806 --> 00:24:11,681
You've really got a way with words.

265
00:24:12,083 --> 00:24:14,375
You wouldn't understand.
You're not a son-in-law.

266
00:24:14,829 --> 00:24:16,871
Having a mother-in-law is great.

267
00:24:18,371 --> 00:24:20,038
You really do look alike.

268
00:24:20,399 --> 00:24:23,107
Your eyes crinkle just like my dad's.

269
00:24:24,130 --> 00:24:26,297
You look like my mom too.

270
00:24:26,916 --> 00:24:28,083
Me?

271
00:24:28,750 --> 00:24:30,000
My birth mother.

272
00:24:31,583 --> 00:24:34,166
Your eyes, your nose.

273
00:24:36,291 --> 00:24:39,625
I was a little surprised at first.
I couldn't tell anyone, though.

274
00:24:45,291 --> 00:24:50,166
I'm holding
seven-year-old Ji Hu right now.

275
00:24:55,029 --> 00:24:58,570
And I'm holding
middle-schooler Ji Ni right now.

276
00:25:19,123 --> 00:25:20,807
I want to see the ocean.

277
00:25:22,188 --> 00:25:24,083
Me too.

278
00:25:24,208 --> 00:25:25,500
Let's go to Sokcho too.

279
00:25:26,458 --> 00:25:28,291
Should we?

280
00:25:28,791 --> 00:25:30,875
Okay. Let's go see the beach too.

281
00:25:31,291 --> 00:25:35,375
We'll go to the beach
and scream our hearts out.

282
00:25:35,958 --> 00:25:41,291
I miss my daughter, Ji Ni,
and I miss Ji Hu too.

283
00:25:44,748 --> 00:25:46,623
I'll call us a cab.

284
00:25:46,625 --> 00:25:49,041
We're going.

285
00:25:49,125 --> 00:25:50,906
I'll call one.

286
00:25:50,908 --> 00:25:52,297
Let's go, let's go!

287
00:25:57,134 --> 00:25:59,104
Ji Ni.

288
00:25:59,843 --> 00:26:04,333
Ji Hu, I'm here!

289
00:26:05,474 --> 00:26:10,583
Ji Ni, I came because I was lonely.

290
00:26:11,541 --> 00:26:14,291
Ji Ni!

291
00:26:16,708 --> 00:26:18,333
Ji Hu...

292
00:26:19,500 --> 00:26:20,750
Mother.

293
00:26:22,125 --> 00:26:25,291
Son-in-law.

294
00:26:25,916 --> 00:26:29,875
Ji Ni, I'm here!

295
00:26:33,458 --> 00:26:36,166
Ji Ni.

296
00:26:36,291 --> 00:26:41,250
Is Ji Ni asleep?

297
00:26:41,791 --> 00:26:47,166
My poor, lonely girl.

298
00:26:47,333 --> 00:26:51,500
I'm here!

299
00:26:55,899 --> 00:26:56,941
Mom.

300
00:26:57,208 --> 00:27:01,375
My beautiful girl. I'm so happy.

301
00:27:04,687 --> 00:27:10,937
My sweet Ji Ni, I was wrong.

302
00:28:11,041 --> 00:28:16,166
Jung A.

303
00:28:16,375 --> 00:28:19,458
Jung A!

304
00:28:55,375 --> 00:28:58,665
(Family Register)

305
00:28:58,666 --> 00:29:00,125
Why are you being so nice to me?

306
00:29:00,166 --> 00:29:02,000
We're supposed to be enemies.

307
00:29:02,041 --> 00:29:03,958
What's that noise? Was this here before?

308
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:05,041
This is my house.

309
00:29:05,083 --> 00:29:07,791
I'm the owner,
so don't get too comfortable here.

310
00:29:07,833 --> 00:29:11,416
If I take sides,
both sides will get mad at me.

311
00:29:11,458 --> 00:29:13,375
- The name.
- I said it had "Cheol" in it.

312
00:29:13,416 --> 00:29:15,666
- I'll make sure you get it. I promise.
- By the end of this week.

313
00:29:15,708 --> 00:29:17,625
I know exactly
where your daughter got married.

314
00:29:17,666 --> 00:29:19,541
I know her studio
and the publishing house too.

315
00:29:20,838 --> 00:29:22,838
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
